results(EXP-VNC-01, "V = min(g,c,t,m) discrimination via per-axis breakers + NC ablations"):

  attractor:
    healthy_V: 0.1019
    g: 0.1019   c: 1.000   t: 1.000   m: 1.000

  V_table:
    //  scenario                          g      c      t      m      V
    "healthy kernel"                   0.102  1.000  1.000  1.000  0.102
    "NC-01 (gov=0, no S5)"             0.000  1.000  1.000  1.000  0.000
    "NC-02 (trust=0.5 const)"          0.102  1.000  1.000  1.000  0.102
    "NC-03 (no S2, SV same)"           0.102  1.000  1.000  1.000  0.102
    "g_break (A0 violation)"           0.000  1.000  1.000  1.000  0.000
    "c_break (a=1.010)"                0.102  0.000  1.000  1.000  0.000
    "t_break (N=4 square orbit β₁=1)"  0.102  1.000  0.000  1.000  0.000
    "m_break (random cap probe ℝ¹²⁸)"  0.102  1.000  1.000  0.000  0.000

  H_VNC1: CONFIRMED  // ∃ configuration with V≈0 (multiple confirmed)

  H_VNC2: CONFIRMED  // each axis independently drives V→0
    g_axis: "A0 violation: dims[53]=1.0 → g=0 → V=0"
    c_axis: "a=1.010 → λ_max=ln(1.010)=0.00995>0 → expanding dynamics → c=0 → V=0"
    t_axis: "N=4 square orbit in dims 116,117: d_adj=0.2000 < ε=0.30, d_diag=0.4000 > ε.
             No triangles possible (diagonals > ε). β₁=1 (hole) → t=0 → V=0."
    m_axis: "Random unit vectors in ℝ¹²⁸ probing Ω_A={cos≥0.70}. By CLT on the unit
             sphere, σ_cos ≈ 1/√128 ≈ 0.088 << 0.70 → P(cos≥0.70)≈0.
             confinement=0.0000 → m=0 → V=0."

  H_VNC3: CONFIRMED
    NC-01_V: 0.000  // governed=0 → g=0 (no S5 governance)
    NC-02_V: 0.102  // trust=0.5 constant — still viable (trust dims reduced but g=0.102 from A3_cpu)
    NC-03_V: 0.102  // no S2 channels — structurally same SV → V unchanged (S2 absence not in SV directly)

  t_break_geometry:
    N: 4
    radius: 2.207   // = sv0_norm * 0.50
    d_adj: 0.2000   // cosine_distance between adjacent square vertices (< ε=0.30 ✓)
    d_diag: 0.4000  // cosine_distance between opposite vertices (> ε=0.30 ✓)
    triangles: 0    // diagonals exceed ε → no triangles → β₁=1 guaranteed
    beta_1: 1

  m_break_geometry:
    method: "spherical cap probe — random uniform unit vectors in ℝ¹²⁸"
    n_samples: 5000
    confinement: 0.0000
    sigma_cos: 0.088  // 1/sqrt(128) — CLT on unit sphere
    cap_fraction: 0.0  // P(Z > 0.70/0.088) ≈ 0 (threshold >> σ)

  interpretation:
    "V = min(g,c,t,m) is a DISCRIMINATING viability certificate: a single axis failure
     is necessary and sufficient to drive V=0. Each of the 4 axes can independently cause
     failure. NC ablations confirm the NC design: NC-01 (no governance) gives V=0 via g,
     while NC-02/NC-03 (structural modifications without actual violations) leave V=0.102
     — they remain viable. The certifier-validation suite is complete."
